WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.830
SPEAKER: Cloud
storage costs money.

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.600
And unless you're
made of money, you'll

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.820
want to understand how
to optimize your spending

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:08.830
to match your data
storage and serving needs.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.130
As a fellow human who's
not made of money,

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.590
let's talk about those
fees, your options,

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.900
and the importance of
budgeting in cloud storage.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.194
[JAZZ MUSIC]

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.070
Just like a grocery run
on an empty stomach,

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.650
a budget can help you keep
your cloud computing and food

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.570
bills from getting surprising.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:34.830
Let's look at how pricing
breaks down for cloud storage.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:37.470
To start, cloud storage
pricing is based

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.420
on the following components--

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:41.760
data storage, which
is the amount of data

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.320
stored in your buckets.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.260
The rates will vary depending on
the storage class of your data

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.660
and the location
of your buckets.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.030
Retrieval and early
deletion fees--

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:52.680
those are applicable
for data stored

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.530
outside of standard
storage classes.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.460
And network usage-- the amount
of data read from or moving

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.620
around between your buckets.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.280
Operations usage are the actions
you take in cloud storage,

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.280
like listing objects
in your buckets.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.640
And remember, there are four
different storage types,

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.160
and the less frequently
you access that storage,

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.080
the less you pay to store it.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.660
Cost for all four is
based upon at rest

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.750
per location, which is a fun
way of saying the cost is

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.730
determined by where the
data lives when it's

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:27.570
just chilling in storage and not
where it's actually being used.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:29.910
For standard storage,
the monthly cost

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:32.460
is the only cost you
need to plan for.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.490
However, with the other
three storage types,

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:38.280
you'll want to consider the
minimum duration of that data,

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.920
as well as any retrieval costs.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:44.730
For example, coldline storage
has a minimum storage duration

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:49.170
of 90 days and a retrieval
cost of, say, two pennies.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.750
So the cheaper monthly
cost is completely worth

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:55.470
it if you only want to access
this data about twice a year.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.650
If, however, you find
yourself accessing or updating

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:00.600
the data every
week, you'll end up

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.760
spending more money
than if you had selected

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.250
standard storage to begin with.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.440
When discussing
network costs, we also

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.530
need to distinguish
between egress and ingress.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.975
Egress represents the data
sent from cloud storage,

00:02:12.975 --> 00:02:15.510
like when reading
data, and ingress

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:18.180
represents the data sent
to cloud storage, like when

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.710
writing data.

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:22.410
Network ingress is always free.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:26.040
For network egress, there are
three categories to consider.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.160
First, when that network
egress is moving or copying

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.380
data to other cloud
storage buckets,

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.590
or when other Google Cloud
services access that data,

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:37.680
this is considered network
egress within Google Cloud,

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:41.550
and is free within regions such
as reading data in a US East

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.940
1 bucket into a US
BigQuery data set.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.970
Pricing then applies for
egress between regions

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:50.100
or across continents.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:53.250
Second, if you use certain
Google Cloud network products,

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:55.920
such as Cloud CDN or
Cloud Interconnect,

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.430
egress pricing is based
on their pricing tables.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:02.460
All other egress is considered
to be general network usage

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:05.490
and is built based upon which
continent the data is traveling

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:06.300
to.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.630
The fourth factor to consider
with billing is operations.

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:12.600
Operation charges apply
when you perform operations

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.430
within Cloud Storage.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:17.070
To clarify, an
operation is an action

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:19.140
that makes changes
to or retrieves

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:23.190
information about buckets
and objects in Cloud Storage.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:26.100
Operations are divided
into three categories--

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.730
Class A, Class B, and free.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.530
For a full list
of the operations

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:35.040
that fall into each class,
check the documentation.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.190
As a brief overview,
Class A includes creating

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.530
storage buckets and objects.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:43.680
Class B includes
retrieving storage objects.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:47.340
And free operations are
primarily deletions.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:50.070
To build your own budget
with accurate cost estimates,

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:51.960
check out the
Pricing Calculator.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:55.170
And for more information
or to see specific costs,

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:58.440
please be sure to check out
the documentation linked below.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.270
Having a budget
will help you plan,

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:02.970
as there's so much more that
you can do with Cloud Storage,

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.190
but that's all for
another episode.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:07.257
Subscribe, give
us a Like, and let

00:04:07.257 --> 00:04:09.090
us know what features
of Cloud Storage you'd

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.620
like to learn more about.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.170
Thanks for joining us for this
quick bite of Cloud Storage.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:16.220
